        "# Project title and aim\n",
        "**Explainable AI for Sea Ice Roughness Prediction Using Sentinel-3 Waveform Features**\n",
        "\n",
        "This project uses machine learning and explainable AI to study sea ice roughness from Sentinel-3 waveform features. The main aim is to find which input features are most important for predicting sea ice roughness. I first train regression models using all input features. Then I use three explainable AI methods to compare feature importance: polynomial regression coefficients, SHAP values from a neural network, and ARD length-scales from Gaussian Process Regression. Finally, I retrain the model using only selected important features and compare the performance with the original full-feature model.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "pPibAPnuUh0V"
      }
    },
