        "This section compares the important features identified by different model interpretation methods. Random Forest importance, polynomial regression coefficients, neural network SHAP values, and Gaussian Process ARD length-scales measure feature influence in different ways. Instead of relying on one method only, I combine the feature rankings across the models. Features that are repeatedly ranked highly are treated as more robust important features."
